## GAP-B2-nonident-narrow — union narrowing for NON-ident (field-access) subjects.
##
## B2 (cce47a0d) recovered a union member only for IDENT/param subjects. This
## extends the narrowed-read machinery to field-access (`s.u`) subjects:
## `if s.u is Int { return s.u }` must recover the MEMBER value (8), not the union
## CELL pointer (~garbage).
##
## A union field is stored as B1/B3's runtime tagged `{tag@0, payload@1}` cell.
## The narrowed read must reload the field's access path and take payload@1, keyed
## on the access-path narrowing stamp (not just NODE_IDENT).
##
## Compile + run:
##   ./self-hosted/bin/quartz spec/qz/gap_b2_field_narrow_smoke.qz > /tmp/gb.ll
##   llc /tmp/gb.ll -filetype=obj -o /tmp/gb.o
##   clang /tmp/gb.o -o /tmp/gb -lm -lpthread && /tmp/gb; echo "exit=$?"
## Expected: prints "field recovered 8" and exits 8.

struct S
  u: Int | String
end

def field_narrow(): Int
  var s = S { u: 0 }
  s.u = 8
  if s.u is Int
    puts("field recovered #{str_from_int(s.u)}")
    return s.u
  end
  puts("FAIL: field is Int did not narrow")
  return 99
end

def main(): Int
  return field_narrow()
end
